        {
          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mt3m26ke58x12jfw",
          "message": {
            "text": "The focused browser matrix independently catches missing and invented chrome. Live Chromium moved the authored vertical thumb from y=33 to 70 to 109 at top/mid/max, placed RTL chrome at x=40 instead of LTR x=172, scaled both-axis marker bounds exactly at DPR 2, and painted no width:none pixels while the current SVG emitted two legacy pills. These controls prevent a large-canvas score or one host palette from hiding wrong activation/geometry.",
            "markdown": "The focused browser matrix independently catches missing and invented chrome. Live Chromium moved the authored vertical thumb from y=33 to 70 to 109 at top/mid/max, placed RTL chrome at x=40 instead of LTR x=172, scaled both-axis marker bounds exactly at DPR 2, and painted no width:none pixels while the current SVG emitted two legacy pills. These controls prevent a large-canvas score or one host palette from hiding wrong activation/geometry."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "docs/165-native-scrollbar-layout-paint-ownership-audit.md"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 424,
                  "endLine": 429,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "The strict gate should compare author marker bounds within one device pixel and\nnative strip pixels exactly or under a reviewed platform-specific raster\nenvelope. It must also mutate every activation to its nearest negative, assert\nthat `--hide-scrollbars` causes the expected explicit no-ink state, reject a\nmissing platform fingerprint, reject any native raster crop outside its\nsource-owned frame, and reject any emitted legacy 7 px synthesized thumb."
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
